WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.460
10 Serbian police officers face charges of torturing protesters, raising prospects for renewed EU accession talks. This is Omni View, episode 227. Malawi's economic mood, a Korean container ship in Arctic waters, and fighting in Yemen come next, then understanding the issue. Serbia's Interior Ministry confirmed nine serving officers and one former officer were detained after accusations they used excessive force against students during 2025 protests.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:28.620
Governments.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:34.400
Coverage Al Jazeera ties to a broader push to reform state institutions under the new government

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:39.220
after incidents in a government compound garage in Belgrade in August 2025.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:44.820
The ministry said the suspects belong to an elite unit and are accused of using force

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:49.460
and threats to inflict severe pain and suffering on several injured people in order to obtain

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:55.260
information, intimidate them, and unlawfully punish them, and it released only the officers'

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:56.000
initials.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.360
Among the detainees, state broadcaster radio television of Serbia said, was Igor Smirak,

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:04.780
commander of the Special Anti-Terrorism Unit.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:09.660
The detentions follow last month's parliamentary elections in which a student-led movement

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:15.260
defeated former president Alexander Vucic after years of anti-corruption demonstrations that

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:21.280
began when the canopy at a railway station in Novisad collapsed in November 2024, killing

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:25.880
including 16 people, a collapse scene as symptomatic of alleged widespread corruption

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:30.780
under Vuchich, who served as president for 12 years before conceding defeat last month.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:36.000
The winning student-led protest movement has demanded reforms within state institutions,

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:42.600
including the police and intelligence services, and Amnesty International's 2025 report documented

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:46.920
repeated cases of excessive force and surveillance against protesters and journalists.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:51.460
With the rights group saying protesters were subjected to excessive force in multiple

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:57.260
cases across the country, protesters have also called on top officials to resign, accusing

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:02.100
them of colluding with Vuchich while he was in power, so on the terms set by that movement,

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:06.000
elite unit detentions leave the demand over senior collusion unmet.

00:02:06.997 --> 00:02:12.817
Malawi, in all Africa's account of a new Afro-Beramater poll, is a country where six and ten people

00:02:12.817 --> 00:02:18.197
believe things are heading in the wrong direction. Respond in sighted food shortages, lack of income,

00:02:18.457 --> 00:02:23.817
and rising living costs as their primary concerns. Not enough to eat, no wage coming in,

00:02:23.997 --> 00:02:28.937
and prices that keep climbing. And the survey captures household-level strain in a country where

00:02:28.937 --> 00:02:34.777
many families already face chronic food insecurity. Meaning hunger is a regular condition rather than

00:02:34.777 --> 00:02:41.337
a one-season shock. Afro-barometer is a long-running continental survey project that tracks attitudes

00:02:41.337 --> 00:02:46.977
across dozens of African states, and the published findings avoid pinning the discontent on a single

00:02:46.977 --> 00:02:52.917
policy, stressing instead how widely it runs. The poll reflects ongoing economic pressures,

00:02:53.117 --> 00:02:56.677
including cash shortages that affect daily life for ordinary households,

00:02:57.237 --> 00:03:02.057
so even routine purchases become hard when notes and coin are simply not there to use.

00:03:02.909 --> 00:03:09.089
Panstar Acro, a South Korean container ship, finished a round trip from Busan to Rotterdam via the

00:03:09.089 --> 00:03:14.849
northern Seerude in 50 days, a voyage Deutscheweller records as saving at least 10 days compared

00:03:14.849 --> 00:03:17.889
with the fastest travel times along the Suez Canal Road.

00:03:18.409 --> 00:03:24.189
The northern Seerude is around 7,000 km shorter, and avoids the geopolitical flashpoint

00:03:24.189 --> 00:03:29.089
of the Middle East, and the vessel left the South Korean port of Busan on August 22.

00:03:29.769 --> 00:03:35.129
Navigated around Russia to the southern British port of Felixto, continued to Rotterdam in

00:03:35.129 --> 00:03:40.149
Netherlands and Gdansk in Poland, then headed back along the same Arctic passage with ice

00:03:40.149 --> 00:03:43.489
breaker support, consistent with current Arctic conditions.

00:03:44.009 --> 00:03:48.389
Western European governments worry that closer commercial ties with Russia could undermine

00:03:48.389 --> 00:03:53.429
sanctions pressure, while Seoul hopes a working economic relationship might give it leverage

00:03:53.429 --> 00:03:58.889
to discourage Russian armed supplies to North Korea, including hoped for influence over Vladimir

00:03:58.889 --> 00:04:01.949
Putin alongside the route's economic potential.

00:04:01.949 --> 00:04:02.629
Council.

00:04:02.629 --> 00:04:08.249
According to the Arctic Council, last year saw a record 1,812 vessels operating in the

00:04:08.249 --> 00:04:12.089
Arctic, an increase of 40 percent compared to 2013.

00:04:13.363 --> 00:04:18.383
Yemen's internationally recognized government, one month into Operation Dawn of Yemen, has

00:04:18.383 --> 00:04:22.523
seen fighting settle into a pattern of incremental territorial gains and losses.

00:04:23.103 --> 00:04:28.283
And Al-Jazeera reports that Sanaa remains largely calm aside from occasional airstrikes.

00:04:28.283 --> 00:04:33.423
When news broke on October 5th that the government was launching a major new offensive to take

00:04:33.423 --> 00:04:38.923
control of territories held by Houthi fighters, residents began to prepare for the worst, and

00:04:38.923 --> 00:04:43.903
Houthi forces have since scored territorial gains in other provinces, including ties

00:04:43.903 --> 00:04:47.363
and Lahige in southern Yemen, where fighting has not ceased.

00:04:47.983 --> 00:04:52.923
Houthi forces have adapted by shifting supply lines and leveraging terrain, while government

00:04:52.923 --> 00:04:58.243
and Saudi-backed forces have disrupted some maritime routes near the Bab al-Mandab Strait,

00:04:58.243 --> 00:05:03.243
the narrow mouth of the Red Sea, and local residents' interview describe reduced immediate fear

00:05:03.243 --> 00:05:08.523
of urban combat. Turkey al-Goblan, head of the Saudi Daimuma Center for Studies,

00:05:09.143 --> 00:05:12.543
argues the operation has weakened three pillars of Houthi logistics,

00:05:12.983 --> 00:05:17.823
while also saying the Houthis have survived in previous years by adapting to strikes and leveraging

00:05:17.823 --> 00:05:23.143
complex geography, clandestine supply and concealment networks, and the use of

00:05:23.143 --> 00:05:27.603
civilians as human shields. The first pillar, according to him, is the fuel and

00:05:27.603 --> 00:05:32.903
supply system, which keeps Houthi combat vehicles moving, transports ammunition and

00:05:32.903 --> 00:05:37.943
delivers reinforcements, and the second is the maritime areas around the Bab al-Mandebs

00:05:37.943 --> 00:05:42.123
straight, and the western coast, outlets through which alternative external

00:05:42.123 --> 00:05:47.711
supply routes pass. Chinese scientists used a robotic arm on the Tian Gong Space

00:05:47.711 --> 00:05:52.551
station to make millimeter scale cuts on large-scale equipment via remote laser.

00:05:52.991 --> 00:05:58.211
A test the South China Morning Post presents as a world-first demonstration of inorbit maintenance

00:05:58.211 --> 00:05:58.951
technology.

00:05:59.331 --> 00:06:04.191
The official science and technology daily reported on Wednesday that a laser maintenance

00:06:04.191 --> 00:06:08.911
device, operated remotely from hundreds of kilometers away, performed that millimeter

00:06:08.911 --> 00:06:12.551
scale work, emphasizing accuracy and remote control.

00:06:12.551 --> 00:06:17.811
role. Precision laser cutting involves focusing a beam of light to slice or melt material with

00:06:17.811 --> 00:06:22.791
extreme accuracy, and the test marks the first time precision laser cutting has been carried

00:06:22.791 --> 00:06:29.401
out in orbit. Open AI pledged to pay for power used by its data centers, solicit local input

